# IntegraIntake

## Stack

Python 3.12+, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy 2 (async), Alembic, Pydantic v2, Docker Compose, pytest, structlog. Custom agent loop — no LangChain.

## Workflow

1. Read current files and understand the scope before changing code.
2. Write a plan (files, changes, tests, risks). Wait for user approval.
3. Implement on a feature branch (`feat/...`, `fix/...`).
4. One commit = one idea. Format: `feat|fix|test|docs|chore(scope): message`.
5. Run tests and verify commands for the change.
6. Keep diffs focused — max ~5 files changed per session when possible.

## Rules

- Engine stays tenant-agnostic; domain behavior lives in YAML under `examples/` (e.g. `freight-broker.yaml`, `repair-service.yaml`).
- LLM proposes; deterministic code (PolicyEngine) decides. Never trust YAML or message body for permissions.
- `tenant_id` comes only from API key/JWT, never from request body.
- No MCP, RAG, or multi-agent until the core intake loop and policy layer are in place.
